{
  "bridge_text": "莉娜踩着冻硬的草地，朝那棵会低声嗡鸣的大树走去；树皮里藏着一个不肯安静的秘密，正等着她去听。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "在村子边上，立着一棵比教堂还高的空心树。每个冬夜，树皮里都会传出低低的嗡鸣，大人们总说：别碰那棵树。可奶奶还没讲完故事就睡着了，莉娜披上红色羊毛外套，穿过结霜的田野，去听那声音。"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "她在树洞里看见一段盘旋向下的楼梯，最上面的台阶上坐着一只老灰狐狸，身上穿着打补丁的绿色背心。他叫莫斯，声音像干叶子一样沙沙的，说这棵树不是用来拜访的，叫她回家，把嗡鸣忘掉。莉娜说，她不能忘记自己还没听见的东西。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The fox in the patched green vest is Mosk, and his dry-leaf voice still hangs in the hollow tree. Lina has heard his warning, yet she stands her ground beside the stair.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, but Lina did not turn away. She reached into her pocket and found the last apple of the season, round and gold in the dark. She set it on the step between them and said it was for the trouble of walking her down."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, as still as a stone. Then he gave a small nod, tied his vest a little tighter, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. Lina followed after him into the deep, quiet below."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The stairs had been waiting in the hush, and now Mosk had taken the first step at last. Below, the faint humming from the tree seemed to call them onward.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs the humming grew softer, like a song heard through sleep. Lina followed Mosk into the dim hollow, where the air smelled of moss and old wood."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "There, on a bed of moss, lay a firefly the size of a robin, her light nearly gone. Mosk’s whiskers trembled. She had once been his friend, he whispered, and one winter long ago he had failed to bring her medicine in time."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "He had guarded the tree ever since, ashamed to face her. Lina knelt beside the moss and asked what the firefly queen needed, and the tiny room held its breath."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The apple had done its work, and Mosk was stepping toward the dark stairs at last. Below him, the hollow tree still hummed softly, waiting in the dimness.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and said it was for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs the humming was a quiet song, and a firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of moss. Her glow was almost out. Mosk's whiskers trembled. She had been his friend once, he whispered, and one winter long ago he had failed to bring her medicine in time. He had been guarding the tree ever since, ashamed to face her."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied, and the humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}
